# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# NOTE: these strings are sourced by bash, so they MUST be free of backticks and the dollar sign (they
# trigger command/parameter substitution). Use plain quotes and the word 'cap' instead.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_owner_sweep_bounded.py" "OWNER-SWEEP-BOUNDED GATE: PASS" "owner cross-tenant sweeps bounded per call (audit P2-2, Marketplace-scale)" "owner sweeps BOUNDED per call (audit P2-2): the cross-tenant owner-context sweeps in 95_owner.sql / 35_lifecycle.sql visited EVERY account sequentially (O(N accounts)) -- owner_cost_surface (~6 queries/account), owner_graph_freshness_surface (the /freshz + /readyz + watchdog freshness input) and prune_all_accounts_with_authority (retention). Going public on the Marketplace grows the account count, so these degrade (/freshz slow, watchdog tick lags, one giant retention transaction holds locks the whole run). FIX: the READ lenses CAP (advisory/visibility -- the ENFORCED quota wall is _account_over_quota at the gate, not these): owner_graph_freshness_surface(p_cap) emits at most p_cap coordinates + visits at most p_cap accounts oldest-ingested-first (mirrors the app-layer VERIPSA_GRAPH_FRESHNESS_CAP=100 the only caller already slices); owner_cost_surface(p_cap) bounds the per-account detail scan but keeps account_count EXACT (a cheap count over the no-RLS routing map) and db_total_bytes EXACT (one size call) so the disk-fill alert + the true fleet total are never bounded away. RETENTION must stay COMPLETE so it is PAGINATED not capped: prune_all_accounts_with_authority(..., p_max_accounts, p_after) does bounded work per call (<= p_max_accounts tenants, each its own txn) and retention_prune.py pages account_id-ascending with the returned next_after cursor until done -- the union of the bounded chunks equals the one-shot sweep (a 1-arg/2-arg call is the EXACT prior sweep). Proven (real DB, N=24 tenants, cap=5): (1) BOUNDED freshness <= cap coords + scanned <= cap; (2) BOUNDED cost scan <= cap yet account_count == N exact + db_total_bytes exact; (3) COMPLETE-but-batched retention visits every tenant exactly once (gap-free) + prunes the SAME rows as one-shot, recent telemetry kept; (4) ISOLATION preserved -- a buyer role is DENIED all three (owner-only; the cap did not widen the cross-tenant boundary); (5) CONTENT-FREE -- no telemetry file path leaks." "owner cross-tenant sweeps do BOUNDED work per call at large N: read lenses cap (account_count + db_total_bytes stay exact), retention paginates to full coverage, isolation preserved (buyer denied all three), content-free" 20
